  acestep.cpp
    https://github.com/ServeurpersoCom/acestep.cpp
    Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The acestep.cpp authors

    Most of the C++ inference path under src/acestep/ is ported from this
    project's ggml implementation rather than written against the PyTorch
    reference directly:

      src/acestep/philox.h              from src/philox.h (verbatim)
      src/acestep/lm_pipeline.{h,cpp}   from src/sampling.h (sample_top_k_p,
                                        verbatim), src/prompt.h, pipeline-lm
      src/acestep/bpe_tokenizer.{h,cpp} from src/bpe.h
      src/acestep/metadata_fsm.h        from src/metadata-fsm.h
      src/acestep/lm_ggml.{h,cpp}       from src/qwen3-lm.h
      src/acestep/textenc_ggml.cpp      from src/qwen3-enc.h
      src/acestep/cond_ggml.{h,cpp}     from src/cond-enc.h
      src/acestep/detok_ggml.{h,cpp}    from src/fsq-detok.h
      src/acestep/dit_ggml.{h,cpp}      from src/dit-graph.h and src/dit*.h
      scripts/convert-acestep-to-gguf.py         from convert.py
      scripts/download-acestep-checkpoints.sh    from checkpoints.sh
      src/acestep/quantize_policy.h and
      src/acestep/quantize_cli.cpp               from tools/quantize.cpp

    The stage GGUFs this engine loads follow that project's layout, and
    src/acestep/engine.cpp follows its pipeline wiring and LM sampling
    defaults so the two implementations can be compared tensor by tensor.

